{"id": "EUVD-2026-81700", "enisaUuid": "bf2aabc4-796f-34dd-8195-54cffeab5be7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: free pending qentry in smc_llc_flow_stop() before memset\n\nsmc_llc_flow_stop() resets a flow struct with a blind memset:\n\n\tspin_lock_bh(&lgr->llc_flow_lock);\n\tmemset(flow, 0, sizeof(*flow));\n\tflow->type = SMC_LLC_FLOW_NONE;\n\tspin_unlock_bh(&lgr->llc_flow_lock);\n\nIf flow->qentry is non-NULL at this point the pointer is overwritten without the\nallocation being freed, leaking one kmalloc object.\n\nA late-arriving duplicate CONFIRM_LINK or ADD_LINK_CONT message can set\nflow->qentry after the legitimate message has been consumed by the waiter via\nsmc_llc_flow_qentry_clr() (which NULLs the pointer but leaves flow->type\nnon-zero) but before the flow completes and smc_llc_flow_stop() runs.  In that\nwindow the duplicate is stashed into flow->qentry, and then lost when\nsmc_llc_flow_stop() zeros the struct.\n\nCall smc_llc_flow_qentry_del() inside the lock before the memset.\nsmc_llc_flow_qentry_del() already checks flow->qentry before freeing, so the\nnormal case where no entry is pending is a no-op.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:58:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e3deb150a5237b672c4579e69a6deb02027dbed", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11bc373ee6630709f0c2da2e7860c23d503c9e9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/032aec7d03c9102616b98fea74f8f7145e7f867c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/957dba2b8b5aebfe09caa6a6b22b958079082eab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f03aa5d36ae3c4068a1c3885146be99aa7fd9307", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0879ea157acc1ac6752f6fcb755d1f91a2359238", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ff429dd6725fa6c1e17a4ed0be8ab675f67a98b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ee0ceddc7785c6dcf4a8107fef01f0414a354f4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mw8r-cvfc-f297", "CVE-2026-90107"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "24e4d30a-ca63-3e69-8d46-3a7ebc3723c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "343d2902-b3b3-34c1-be4c-f3273974369c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <0879ea157acc1ac6752f6fcb755d1f91a2359238"}, {"id": "36e31434-45e7-37bf-97ac-bfb3b3759dc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "39580c70-6618-3ce2-b9f9-c5641586690a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "3a1920f2-8452-33ef-9246-ec5ff37abf4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <5ee0ceddc7785c6dcf4a8107fef01f0414a354f4"}, {"id": "3ff35a91-9d3d-3887-8794-ea753ea9567d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "41ec565a-714b-3862-be72-e309524d04e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <032aec7d03c9102616b98fea74f8f7145e7f867c"}, {"id": "4451e307-ee40-31d4-aae1-edcdf934fc15", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <957dba2b8b5aebfe09caa6a6b22b958079082eab"}, {"id": "4576b999-cb79-3cdb-9753-2f8c671708b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "74025faa-72b5-3367-8f98-be0b2d688262", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b0910f7c-bb5d-300e-9e61-ee11a2f1df2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b40cd678-7002-378b-ba7c-3867215ace54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "b4a4d5dd-70ec-35df-8d14-1ac27268abc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ca444c83-f478-3131-bd44-d53df085477e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <5ff429dd6725fa6c1e17a4ed0be8ab675f67a98b"}, {"id": "d4117cd8-eefe-3577-9f44-2b5e30172097", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "df54b39d-0b30-37f6-a849-8f8847701928", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <f03aa5d36ae3c4068a1c3885146be99aa7fd9307"}, {"id": "ea27eb0b-4cd6-33d3-8ab6-f1a7e6a2b301", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <8e3deb150a5237b672c4579e69a6deb02027dbed"}, {"id": "fc4c27d9-64be-3d7e-b105-1aef8c5a98a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "555da9af827d95134656fa459c8f3ece04dd867a <11bc373ee6630709f0c2da2e7860c23d503c9e9d"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e35f06c9-b413-3894-9fcf-d38560707041", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}